# The Windows console as libedit sees it.
#
# swipl.exe on a Windows console does not read a terminal description:
# it links a fake termcap, packages/libedit/libedit/src/win_ncurses.c,
# which answers tgetflag/tgetnum/tgetstr from a hard-coded table.  This
# entry is that table, so that the suite can put libedit through the
# same decisions on a Unix pty.  Keep the two in step.
#
# The table says what the console and an Epilog window both do: the
# console with ENABLE_VIRTUAL_TERMINAL_PROCESSING on, the window through
# the xpce terminal.  What matters here is as much what is absent as
# what is present:
#
#   no xenl   the console wraps as soon as the last column is written.
#             An Epilog window defers it, and terminal_setflags() sets
#             the flag for that case alone.
#   no smir   an insert opens cells with ich/ich1 rather than switching
#             the terminal to insert mode, which the console has no
#             sequence for
#   no cud    libedit never asks the description to move down
#   no pt     tabs are never used to move the cursor
#
# Capabilities win_ncurses.c answers that libedit never asks for -- cr,
# cm, do, le -- are left out: its tstr[] table has no entry for them.
#
# lines/cols are what the entry has to say; libedit asks the terminal
# itself (GetConsoleScreenBufferInfo on Windows, TIOCGWINSZ here).
#
swipl-winconsole|the Windows console as libedit sees it,
	am,
	cols#80, lines#25,
	bel=^G,
	clear=\E[H\E[J,
	el=\E[K,
	ed=\E[J,
	home=\E[H,
	il1=\E[L,
	dl1=\E[M,
	cuu1=\E[A,
	cuf1=\E[C,
	cuu=\E[%p1%dA,
	cub=\E[%p1%dD,
	cuf=\E[%p1%dC,
	ich1=\E[@,
	ich=\E[%p1%d@,
	dch1=\E[P,
	dch=\E[%p1%dP,
	hpa=\E[%i%p1%dG,
	kcuu1=\E[A,
	kcud1=\E[B,
	kcuf1=\E[C,
	kcub1=\E[D,
	khome=\E[H,
	kend=\E[F,
	kdch1=\E[3~,
